From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ricardo Pardini <ricardo@pardini.net>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:31:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ata: ahci: READ CAPACITY must return the last LBA, not the
 sector count

- SCSI READ CAPACITY (10/16) returns the address of the last block
- scsi_read_capacity() adds 1 since 5f7c06bdc3c ("scsi: fix disk capacity too small by one sector")
- AHCI emulation returned ata_id_n_sectors(), so AHCI disks are now one sector too big
- Reading that sector times out in AHCI (10 s); ums aborts when the host reads the backup GPT

Fixes: 5f7c06bdc3c ("scsi: fix disk capacity too small by one sector")
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Ricardo Pardini <ricardo@pardini.net>
---
 drivers/ata/ahci.c | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/ata/ahci.c b/drivers/ata/ahci.c
index 38e953ee79c..c806ee55d70 100644
--- a/drivers/ata/ahci.c
+++ b/drivers/ata/ahci.c
@@ -759,8 +759,9 @@ static int ata_scsiop_read_capacity10(struct ahci_uc_priv *uc_priv,
 		return -EPERM;
 	}
 
-	cap64 = ata_id_n_sectors(uc_priv->ataid[pccb->target]);
-	if (cap64 > 0x100000000ULL)
+	/* READ CAPACITY returns the address of the last block */
+	cap64 = ata_id_n_sectors(uc_priv->ataid[pccb->target]) - 1;
+	if (cap64 > 0xffffffffULL)
 		cap64 = 0xffffffff;
 
 	cap = cpu_to_be32(cap64);
@@ -788,7 +789,8 @@ static int ata_scsiop_read_capacity16(struct ahci_uc_priv *uc_priv,
 		return -EPERM;
 	}
 
-	cap = ata_id_n_sectors(uc_priv->ataid[pccb->target]);
+	/* READ CAPACITY returns the address of the last block */
+	cap = ata_id_n_sectors(uc_priv->ataid[pccb->target]) - 1;
 	cap = cpu_to_be64(cap);
 	memcpy(pccb->pdata, &cap, sizeof(cap));
 
